# Denali guest login + club branding — remediation contract

Live path 2026-08-16: marketing header **ورود** → portal OTP login → `/me/profile` → **خروج** → same header login again. Session round-trip worked. Chrome names and login phone prefill did not.

**Gate:** phase **0** (this file) → **1** branding → **2** phone traps → **3** avatar a11y → **4** OTP a11y → **5** polish → **1 addendum** member-chip person label. Phase **1–5** in this pack. No `plugin.id === "denali"` in `updateTour`. Do not rename workspace plugin id `denali`. Do not change WRS hosts.

**Club name vs plugin id:** guests must see **`shenski`** (operator `/settings/branding` → `tenants.theme.displayName`). Plugin id `denali` stays the workspace type. After GL-BRAND-01, empty `displayName` still shows i18n `nav.defaultSiteName` (FA باشگاه / EN Club) — **GL-BRAND-02** is what makes every chrome say **shenski**.

## Product branding rule (GL-BRAND)

Club public name is **tenant branding `displayName`**, set by the operator at **`/settings/branding`** (module `workspace_branding`, PATCH `/settings/branding`). Live club name for this tenant is **`shenski`**.

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Marketing header, login chrome, member-shell brand, public metadata all read `GET /public/tenant-branding` → `displayName` | Hardcode `shenski` / `باشگاه` / `Portal` / `denali` in marketing or portal chrome |
| Empty name: one shared guest fallback (`nav.defaultSiteName`) on every surface | Fallback to `bootstrap.pluginId` (`denali`) or literal `"Portal"` |
| Operator Save on settings persists `tenants.theme.displayName` | Logo upload alone persisting the name (already forbidden — keep) |
| Operator smoke tenant `…014` keeps SMK English branding | Changing WRS host labels (`denali.localhost`) |

Live mismatch (empty `theme.displayName` on club seed):

| Surface | What guest saw | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Marketing header | باشگاه | `displayName ?? t("nav.defaultSiteName")` → FA default |
| Login chrome | Portal | `displayName \|\| "Portal"` in `portal-registration-chrome.tsx` |
| Member `/me` header | denali | `displayName \|\| bootstrap.pluginId` in `app/me/layout.tsx` |

```text
Admin  /settings/branding  →  tenants.theme.displayName = "shenski"
                                    │
         GET /public/tenant-branding.displayName
                    ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
                    ▼               ▼                ▼
              marketing         login chrome      member shell
              brand title       workspace label   workspaceLabel
```

### Phase 1 layers (no product literals in guest apps)

| Layer | Owner | Rule |
| ----- | ----- | ---- |
| Resolve empty name | `guest-surface-host` `resolveGuestChromeDisplayName(displayName, fallback)` | Trimmed `displayName` wins. Else caller i18n. Never `"Portal"`, never `pluginId`. |
| Fetch failure ≠ empty name | `fetchPublicTenantBrandingForHost` | Network / non-OK keeps the last **successful** snapshot for that branding host (process memory). Do not treat an API blip as `displayName: null` (that flashes i18n «باشگاه»). Still never hardcode `shenski`. Successful empty name still uses the i18n fallback. |
| Marketing fallback | `catalog.nav.defaultSiteName` | Call the helper directly (no app-local alias wrapper). |
| Portal fallback | `catalogRegistration.chrome.defaultSiteName` | One portal key (login chrome, `/me` header, document title). **Byte-equal** to marketing `nav.defaultSiteName` (guard spec). |
| Club seed name | `DEV_TENANTS` denali row `…000003` `theme.displayName` | **`shenski`**. Workspace-type default stays color-only so operator smoke `…014` does not inherit the trade name. |
| Postgres club seed | `ProvisioningService.seedDenaliSmokeTenant` | Copies `DEV_TENANTS` theme only behind `canResolveDevTenantRegistryFallback()` (DEC-039 / `guard:static-registry`). That gate is true in **dev and test**, including when `DATABASE_URL` is set, so Phase 6.6 Postgres seed still writes `displayName=shenski`. Production auth mode does not read the static registry and keeps the color-only workspace-type default. |
| Merge | `resolveEffectiveTenantBranding` | Unchanged. Do not inherit `displayName` from workspace-type fallback when stored theme already has colors. |

### Phase 1 addendum — person chip vs club brand (GL-BRAND-03)

Club chrome and the logged-in **person** chip are different labels on the same `/me` header. Mixing them reopens the باشگاه / Portal / denali class of bug as English `"Member"` on the FA portal.

```text
/me header
  ├─ workspaceLabel  → resolveGuestChromeDisplayName(branding.displayName, chrome.defaultSiteName)
  │                    club trade name (shenski) or باشگاه / Club
  └─ member chip     → resolveGuestMemberChipLabel({ displayName, mobile, fallback })
                       chosen personal name only
                       else portalMember.nav.memberFallback  (FA عضو / EN Member)
```

| Surface | Owner | Rule |
| ------- | ----- | ---- |
| Club brand (`data-portal-shell-workspace-label`) | GL-BRAND-01/02 | Unchanged helper. Empty → `defaultSiteName` only. |
| Person chip (`data-marketing-header-member-label`) | **GL-BRAND-03** | Shared `resolveGuestMemberChipLabel`. **Not** a phone number. **Not** English `"Member"` as a placeholder. Empty / placeholder / name-equals-mobile → i18n `memberFallback` (FA **عضو** / EN Member). |
| Login `sessionBadge` | already | Club `branding.displayName` or hidden when empty. Do **not** put `"Member"` or `memberFallback` here (would duplicate chrome). |
| Marketing header chip | same helper | `catalog.nav.memberFallback` is **byte-equal** to portal `portalMember.nav.memberFallback`. No `"Member"` literal in `resolve-marketing-member-header.server.ts`. |

`GET /identity/me` fills `displayName` with `user.mobile` when the membership has no name. That is a directory convenience, not a guest chip label — the helper treats `displayName === mobile` as unnamed. Literal `"Member"` is the old hardcoded fallback and is also unnamed. Do **not** call `resolveGuestChromeDisplayName` for the person chip (`باشگاه` is not a personal name). Do **not** put the US smoke phone on the chip (`guestVisibleProfileMobile` stays for other surfaces).

**`/me/profile` mobile is not the chip.** The profile form is the identity record. `MemberProfileMobileChange` renders `currentMobile={profile.fields.mobile}` at `data-member-profile-mobile-change-value`. An old membership that still holds a test number (`+15550009901`, `09128881147`, …) **must keep showing that stored value**. Do **not** run `guestLoginPhoneFieldValue` / chip sanitizer on this readout — login empty-phone and header-chip rules are different surfaces.

To replace the stored number: **تغییر شماره موبایل** (`portalMember.mobileChange.start`) → OTP to the new phone. The start handler already clears the *new-phone* input (`setPhone("")`); it does not blank the displayed current value until verify succeeds.

```text
identity.mobile  ──►  /me/profile  data-member-profile-mobile-change-value   (stored, always)
                 └──►  header chip  resolveGuestMemberChipLabel               (never the phone)
```

### Phase 2 phone traps

Guest login/register phone is a **blank field**. The US smoke number is a named fixture, never a visible default.

```text
createCatalogRegistrationFlowInitialData.phone
        → initialPublicRegistrationPhone() = ""
                 │
                 ├── Input value  → guestLoginPhoneFieldValue(phone)
                 │                  trim === +15550009901  →  ""
                 ├── autoComplete="off"  →  after logout, browser must not restore the fixture
                 └── OTP «تغییر شماره»  →  phone: ""  (not the initializer, not the fixture)
```

| Rule | Why |
| ---- | --- |
| `initialPublicRegistrationPhone()` is always `""` | Even in `NODE_ENV=development`. Sending OTP without typing must not log into the smoke user. |
| `PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_DEV_PHONE` | Named fixture for API/E2E that **fill** the field. Never `value={PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_DEV_PHONE}`. |
| `guestLoginPhoneFieldValue` | If flow state or autofill injects the fixture, the input shows empty and submit sees empty (`MOBILE_REQUIRED`). Same trim-match as chrome `guestVisibleProfileMobile`. |
| Phone input `autoComplete="off"` | `id="phone"` is an autofill magnet. After **خروج** the field must stay empty, not restore `+15550009901`. |
| OTP «تغییر شماره» | Writes `phone: ""`, not a call back into the initializer. |

Dev OTP hint / `initialPublicRegistrationOtp()` (`1234`) may stay. Do **not** put `autoComplete="tel"` on this field (that reopens the smoke-number restore).

### Phase 3 avatar a11y (GL-AVATAR-01)

```text
[file input]  clip via [data-member-profile-avatar-upload] CSS
      │
      ├── before: aria-label = t("avatarUpload")  →  2nd named control
      └── after:  aria-hidden + tabIndex=-1 + no name
                 button remains the only named upload control
                 button still calls inputRef.click()
```

| Rule | Why |
| ---- | --- |
| Do **not** add `className="sr-only"` / Tailwind hide on `member-profile-avatar.tsx` | File is in I0 shell-appearance scan (`portal-me`). Clip already lives in Denali + starter portal CSS. |
| Do **not** change `apps/web` profile settings | Different surface; not guest `/me/profile`. |
| Spec `MP-A11Y-01` | Preview `role="img"` stays. File input must **not** carry `avatarUpload` as `aria-label`. |

### Phase 4 OTP a11y (GL-OTP-01)

Guest login uses **`packages/catalog-registration-flow-ui/src/otp-segment-input.tsx`** (portal `transpilePackages` + `dist`). Operator login uses `apps/web/src/features/auth/otp-segment-input.tsx`. P6 still requires a thin portal shell at `apps/portal/src/features/auth/otp-segment-input.tsx` — it is **not** on the live guest path.

**v10 live proof:** a clipped native sink with `aria-hidden` + `tabIndex={-1}` + `id="otp"` still mapped as an unnamed `textbox` in the accessibility snapshot. Chromium exposes a programmatically focusable `<input>` even when the host is clipped. Guest SMS autofill therefore binds to the **first visible cell**, not a fifth field.

```text
SMS autofill  →  cell 0  autocomplete=one-time-code  maxLength=4
                 cells 1–3  autocomplete=off          maxLength=1
                 onChange/onPaste already splits a 4-digit dump across cells
                 no data-otp-autofill-sink on the guest path
                 no id="otp" on an input (group may keep the id)
                 cells  →  otp.digitLabel + formatOtpDigitIndex (FA رقم ۱ … ۴)
                 group  →  catalogRegistration.otp.groupLabel
```

| Failure | Cause |
| ------- | ----- |
| Extra unnamed textbox | Fifth native `<input id="otp">` sink. `aria-hidden` on a focusable control is ignored. Guest path **deletes** the sink. |
| English `Digit 1` | Hardcoded `aria-label`. Keys stay under `catalogRegistration.otp`. |
| FA `رقم 1` (Latin index) | `{index}` interpolated as ASCII. `formatOtpDigitIndex` uses `fa-IR` so the name is **رقم ۱**. EN stays `Digit 1`. |
| Caption naming a sink | `<label htmlFor="otp">` is gone. Group `aria-labelledby` owns the name. |

Operator + unused P6 portal shell keep a clipped **ui-primitives `Input`** sink (P3-ENTRY-02 / `guard-no-raw-wizard-input` forbid raw `<input>` in `apps/web`). Inline clip styles still hide it; `aria-hidden` + `tabIndex={-1}` stay. Do **not** reintroduce a guest sink. e2e fills `[data-otp-cell]`. Dev hint `otp.devHint` (`کد توسعه: 1234`) stays.

### Phase 5 polish

| ID | Implementation | Must not |
| -- | -------------- | -------- |
| **GL-POLISH-01** | `apps/portal/public/icon.svg` — same generic teal triangle as marketing `public/icon.svg`. `generateMetadata.icons` + Next rewrite `/favicon.ico` → `/icon.svg`. | Invent a Denali/shenski mark. Rename plugin hosts. |
| **GL-POLISH-02** | First hero slide `fetchPriority="high"` + `loading="eager"`; later slides `low` / `lazy`. Keep native `<img>` so Ken Burns CSS `img[data-marketing-home-hero-slide]` still matches. | Wrap slides in `next/image` `fill` (extra span fights `inset: -4%` / scale). Login blocker. |

```text
Browser  GET /favicon.ico
              │
              ▼
     portal next.config rewrite  →  /icon.svg  (public, generic)
```

